│     I renamed `HTTPParser.complete` to `reset` and added a `keep_alive` property in both the `httpx` and `ahttpx` packages, with the server    │
│ and pool updated to match. I also made server shutdown close streams and swallow `KeyboardInterrupt` in `run()`. The patch is submitted (6     │
│ files changed). I did not run the tests.                                                                                                       │
│                                                                                                                                                │
│     Changes are in `src/httpx/` and `src/ahttpx/`:                                                                                             │
│     - **Parser:** `complete` is now `reset`, and `keep_alive` is a read-only property returning `send_keep_alive and recv_keep_alive`.         │
│     - **Pool:** `_complete` calls `reset()`.                                                                                                   │
│     - **Server `_complete`:** it previously referenced `complete` without calling it. It now drains the request body on keep-alive connections │
│ before resetting the parser.                                                                                                                   │
│     - **Server shutdown:** the request handler closes the connection in a `finally` block. `run()` catches `KeyboardInterrupt`.                │
│                                                                                                                                                │
│     Open risks:                                                                                                                                │
│     - `tests/test_parsers.py` still calls `p.complete()` in five places, so those tests will fail until they are updated to `reset()`. I left  │
│ test files alone as required.                                                                                                                  │
│     - I guessed that `keep_alive` should be a property. If the hidden tests assign to it, this will break.                                     │
│     - The body-drain loop assumes `recv_body()` is safe to call until it returns empty, and I did not verify that.                             │
